{"name":"Envy’s Love","hex":"#2dd78d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"envy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Resentful desire of something possessed by another or others (but not limited to material possessions). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An object of envious notice or feeling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feel displeasure or hatred towards (someone) for their good fortune or possessions.","To resentfully or discontentedly desire (something someone else has that one lacks)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"},{"title":"Envy","blocks":[{"text":"Envy is an emotion which occurs when a person lacks another's quality, skill, achievement, or possession and either desires it or wishes that the other lacked it. Envy can also refer to the wish for another person to lack something one already possesses so as to remove the equality of possession between both parties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg/330px-The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&ut